<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Suwayda</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as As-Suwayda, Sweida</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Suwayda is a city in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, capital of the Suwayda <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/governorate">Governorate</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jabal-al-druze">Jabal al-Druze</a>, whose population is mainly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/druze">Druze</a>. It was the capital of the autonomous Jabal Druze State under the French Mandate and a centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-syrian-revolt">Great Syrian Revolt</a> led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan-al-atrash">Sultan al-Atrash</a> in 1925. The surrounding region has many Roman and Byzantine remains.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/suwayda.jpg" alt="Suwayda" width="320" height="234" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shadi Alashkar · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Swaida_city.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In Syria Sultan Pasha al-Atrash led the Druze in the Syrian Revolution of 1925–27, Adib Shishakli’s government attacked the Jabal al-Druze in the early 1950s, and in 2018 an ISIS-affiliated attack on <b>Suwayda</b> killed at least 258 people.</blockquote><a href="/religion/druze-faith">Druze faith · Legacy</a></li><li><blockquote>The state was renamed Jabal al-Arab, and under the 1936 Franco-Syrian treaty it was joined to the Syrian Republic, becoming the province of <b>Suwayda</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/jabal-druze-state">Jabal Druze State</a></li></ul></section>
